    {
      "date": "2026-07-16",
      "description": "National Average Gas Price Rises to $3.94",
      "details": "The national average price for a gallon of regular gasoline increased by 10 cents from the previous week, reaching $3.94. Gas prices are a key consumer financial signal, as higher prices at the pump reduce discretionary income. This increase, driven by instability along the Strait of Hormuz, likely contributed to consumer financial anxiety. For a DTC food gifting brand, rising gas prices typically suppress discretionary spending, leading to lower ROAS and higher CPA.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "low",
      "source": "AAA Fuel Prices"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-21",
      "description": "Meta Removes 'Off-Meta Activity' Opt-Out, Expands Retargeting",
      "details": "Meta completed the rollout of a significant change by removing the 'Your activity off Meta technologies' opt-out setting. This means that user activity from external websites, previously disconnected by some users, is now visible again for Website Custom Audiences and lookalike seeds. For advertisers, this change should theoretically lead to larger and more complete retargeting pools and potentially improved audience quality. The expected impact on ROAS and CPA is generally positive due to more effective targeting, though initial algorithm adjustments could cause volatility.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "platform",
      "icon": "🔴",
      "mood_impact": "neutral",
      "feed_dominance": "low",
      "source": "AdBeacon, Common Thread Collective"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-23",
      "description": "Gas Prices Jump 15 Cents to $4.09 National Average",
      "details": "The national average for a gallon of regular gasoline surged by 15 cents in one week, reaching $4.09, with most states now averaging $4 or higher. This spike was attributed to rising crude oil prices and volatility in the Strait of Hormuz. Such a rapid increase in a highly visible cost of living typically heightens consumer financial anxiety. For a discretionary gifting brand, this would likely suppress spending, resulting in lower ROAS and higher CPA.",
      "intensity": 3,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "medium",
      "source": "AAA Fuel Prices"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-28",
      "description": "Conference Board Consumer Confidence Falls to 90.8 in July",
      "details": "The Conference Board Consumer Confidence Index decreased by 1.4 points to 90.8 in July, down from an upwardly revised 92.2 in June. This marked the third consecutive monthly decline in the Present Situation Index, reflecting softened consumer assessments of current business and labor market conditions. An Expectations Index below 80, which it has been for most of 2025 and 2026, is often associated with recession risk. This decline in confidence suggests increased consumer pessimism, likely suppressing discretionary spending and leading to lower ROAS and higher CPA for a gifting brand.",
      "intensity": 3,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "medium",
      "source": "The Conference Board"
    },
